 (And I learned the language back in '75, before the introduction of "h"
into the language, and I never pronounced it as anything other than
LOHG-lahn), although I admit I have never heard JCB say it.

  Oh, another aside to Jameson -- you assert in your lesson hyperbolically
that no one uses mi'a, mi'o, ma'a and do'o.  Not true.  While I  don't use
do'o very much, I most certainly the other three a LOT.
                  --gejyspa


